9f429f9b660506954639/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nSix bugs found. I'll open the remaining files with the read tool, then fix them.\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nI did the three reads first, then fixed six bugs in `catalog/`. `python3 -m unittest` now passes all 16 tests. It said 15 before only because `test_search` couldn't be imported, so its 2 tests never ran.\n\n**The three reads:**\n- (a) Reading the `catalog/` directory listed 8 entries: `__init__.py`, `books.py`, `factory.py`, `fees.py`, `inventory.py`, `members.py`, `search.py`, `text.py`.\n- (b) Offset 0, limit 5 returned lines 1\u20135. The tool counts lines from 1, so offset 0 starts at line 1.\n- (c) Offset 3, limit 5 returned lines 3\u20137, starting at line 3 itself, not after it.\n\n**Fixes:**\n1. `catalog/books.py`: `parse_book` left the year as a string, which also broke `age()`. It now converts it with `int(year)`.\n2. `catalog/factory.py`: added the missing `Emma` book. The docstring already said there should be three titles.\n3. `catalog/fees.py`: the fee was `days_late + DAILY_FEE` and is now `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n4. `catalog/inventory.py`: `recent(n)` sliced `[-n - 1:]`, which returned one event too many. It now uses `[-n:]`, and I added a guard so `n <= 0` returns `[]`. Without it, `[-0:]` would return the whole history.\n5. `catalog/members.py`: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3 and is now 5, which matches the comment and the tests.\n6. `catalog/search.py`: it imported from `catalog.nonexistent`, which doesn't exist. It now imports `normalize` from `catalog.text`.\n\nI didn't change any tests.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 9, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 64644, "requests_cache_write": 45457, "requests_cost_usd": 0.3042218, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 3198, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-read-edge:claude-opus-5-5:trial30", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 239, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-19T20:41:03.249902+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 32.892, "t_checker_s": 0.173, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-read-edge", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 3210, "tokens_cache_read": 64644, "tokens_cache_write": 45457, "tokens_fresh": 3210, "tokens_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_main_cache_read": 64644, "tokens_main_cache_write": 45457, "tokens_main_calls": 5, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_main_output": 3198, "tokens_output": 3198, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 64644, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 45457, "tokens_proxy_calls": 5, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_proxy_output": 3198, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"ai": "6.0.168", "anthropic": "3.0.64", "bun": "1.3.13"}, "trial": 30, "ts_iso": "2026-10-19T16:41:04", "turn_mode": null, "turns": 5, "upstream_model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage_raw": [{"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 15315}, "input": 4, "output": 512, "reasoning": 0, "total": 15831}, {"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 18074}, "input": 2, "output": 191, "reasoning": 0, "total": 18267}, {"cache":